  ID MAP (yours already in use: 100500 = PowerShell EncodedCommand)
    100012-100016  Web scanning / recon
    100020-100026  Authentication / brute force
    100030-100039  File integrity / webshell
    100040-100049  Web attack payloads (SQLi, XSS, LFI, cmd injection)
    100050-100059  Network / port scanning
    100060-100069  Linux post-exploitation
    100070-100079  Persistence
    100080-100089  Vulnerability & config posture
    100090-100099  Windows / Sysmon (extends your 100500)
    100110-100119  Tuning / noise control

  IMPORTANT — BUILT-IN SID DEPENDENCIES
    Several rules below chain off Wazuh's default ruleset via <if_sid>.
    Default SIDs shift between ruleset versions. BEFORE you rely on any
    of these, confirm the parent SID on YOUR install:

      sudo /var/ossec/bin/wazuh-logtest
      (paste a real log line, read the "Rule id" it reports)

