  1. Syntax check — the manager will refuse to start on malformed XML:
       sudo /var/ossec/bin/wazuh-logtest

  2. Test a rule against a real log line. Paste the line at the prompt and
     read back the rule id and level it matched:
       sudo /var/ossec/bin/wazuh-logtest
       # e.g. paste an Apache 404 line, confirm 100012 fires

  3. Restart and confirm clean start:
       sudo systemctl restart wazuh-manager
       sudo systemctl status wazuh-manager
       sudo tail -f /var/ossec/logs/ossec.log

  4. If the manager fails to start, the log names the offending rule id:
       sudo grep -i error /var/ossec/logs/ossec.log | tail -20

  ============================================================================
  TUNING NOTES WORTH RECORDING IN YOUR REPORT
  ============================================================================
  - frequency counts events matching the referenced rule within timeframe.
    Verify actual firing thresholds empirically rather than trusting the
    number; behaviour has differed across OSSEC/Wazuh versions.

  - <same_source_ip /> is the legacy form; <same_field>srcip</same_field> is
    current. Both work in 4.x. This file uses the current form.

  - Rules that never fire are worse than noisy rules, because they create
    false confidence. For every rule above that produces nothing during your
    exercise, state in the report whether that is because the behaviour did
    not occur, or because the detection is broken. Those are very different
    findings, and knowing the difference is the actual skill being assessed.
  ============================================================================
-->

<!-- Windows / PowerShell endpoint detections (TICKET-005) -->
<group name="sysmon,windows,powershell,custom,">
  <rule id="100600" level="12">
    <if_sid>61603</if_sid>
    <field name="win.eventdata.commandLine" type="pcre2">(?i)\s-e[a-z]*\s+[A-Za-z0-9+/=]{15,}</field>
    <description>PowerShell: Base64 encoded command executed (T1059.001) on $(win.system.computer)</description>
    <mitre><id>T1059.001</id></mitre>
  </rule>
  <rule id="100601" level="12">
    <if_sid>61603</if_sid>
    <field name="win.eventdata.commandLine" type="pcre2">(?i)(DownloadString|DownloadFile|IEX|Invoke-Expression|Net\.WebClient)</field>
    <description>PowerShell: download cradle / IEX execution (T1059.001) on $(win.system.computer)</description>
    <mitre><id>T1059.001</id></mitre>
  </rule>
  <rule id="100602" level="10">
    <if_sid>61603</if_sid>
    <field name="win.eventdata.commandLine" type="pcre2">(?i)(certutil.*urlcache|certutil.*-f\s+http|bitsadmin.*/transfer)</field>
    <description>LOLBin download attempt (T1105) on $(win.system.computer)</description>
    <mitre><id>T1105</id></mitre>
  </rule>
  <rule id="100603" level="10">
    <if_sid>61614</if_sid>
    <field name="win.eventdata.targetObject" type="pcre2">(?i)\\CurrentVersion\\Run</field>
    <description>Registry Run key persistence set (T1547.001) on $(win.system.computer)</description>
    <mitre><id>T1547.001</id></mitre>
  </rule>
</group>
